From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 12:14:26 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] dt-bindings: soc: apple: sleep: describe power words
 a machine lacks

The sleep controller's driver walks one list of PMGR power state words
per SoC, taken from one machine's device tree. Another machine on the
same SoC may have no power state at some of those offsets.

Add apple,ps-absent and apple,ps-aon-absent to name them, for the main
and the always-on PMGR blocks.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
---
 .../bindings/soc/apple/apple,t8140-sleep.yaml       | 13 +++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+)

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/soc/apple/apple,t8140-sleep.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/soc/apple/apple,t8140-sleep.yaml
index be0f2a31a2..7d82a92d6d 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/soc/apple/apple,t8140-sleep.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/soc/apple/apple,t8140-sleep.yaml
@@ -62,6 +62,19 @@ properties:
       SoC's sleep would raise for the commit but that this machine's macOS
       leaves as they are. They are neither raised nor put back.
 
+  apple,ps-absent:
+    $ref: /schemas/types.yaml#/definitions/uint32-array
+    description:
+      Power state words of the SoC's lists, as offsets into the PMGR power
+      state block, that this machine has no power state for. They are not
+      saved, raised or reported around a sleep. A word of the always-on
+      block that the sleep lowers and that reads on is still lowered.
+
+  apple,ps-aon-absent:
+    $ref: /schemas/types.yaml#/definitions/uint32-array
+    description:
+      As apple,ps-absent, for the always-on PMGR power state block.
+
   apple,debug-port:
     $ref: /schemas/types.yaml#/definitions/phandle
     description:
-- 
